-- title:
--   Re-choosing one local Whittaker factor within its cyclic span
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field whose ring of integers is an integral $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra, let $\psi$ be a continuous additive character of the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and let $\mu$ be a character of the idele group of $K$. Let $D$ be a subset of the adelic $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, $U$ an assignment of a subgroup of that group to each ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\mathrm{gen}$ an assignment of an element to each finite place, and $S$ a set of finite places; the carrier data used throughout is `productionPinsOf ℚ D U gen (AdelicBox.adelicBox ℚ)`, which equips adelic $\mathrm{GL}_2$ with its Borel structure and Haar measure, takes the full central subgroup, retains $D$, $U$ and $\mathrm{gen}$, and uses the adelic additive Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box. Let $X$ be a bundle `CubicInductionData` consisting of a form on adelic $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, a global Whittaker function, a local Whittaker function at each finite place, an archimedean Whittaker function, a central character and a dual Whittaker function, and assume `IsCubicInductionDataOn` holds for $X$ relative to $K$, these pins, $\psi$, $\mu$ and $S$: the form is left invariant under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q})$, transforms under central adelic scalars by the central character, which is trivial on principal ideles; the form is cuspidal along the parabolics of types $(2,1)$ and $(1,2)$; the Whittaker function is the $\psi$-Whittaker transform `whittaker3` of the form, satisfies the $\psi$-Whittaker transformation law, and summing its mirabolic translates recovers the form; the local Whittaker functions satisfy the corresponding local laws for the local components of $\psi$, the Whittaker function factorises as the archimedean value times the product of local values over any finite set of places containing $S$ outside which the component lies in the standard maximal compact, the local factors are induced-spherical with coefficients `inducedCoeff K μ` off $S$, are invariant under the congruence subgroup of the induced level at unramified places off $S$, and satisfy the local multiplicity-one condition; the form has moderate growth, the archimedean Whittaker function is $K$-finite, the form has the iota moments and half-plane properties; and the dual Whittaker function is the $\psi^{-1}$-transform of the dual form, with the analogous law, expansion, moments and half-plane properties. Assume further that the form, the Whittaker function and the dual Whittaker function are continuous, that the latter two are gauge-majorised in the sense of `IsGaugeMajorised3` (there are $t$, a finite set of places $T$ and $B$ such that the function vanishes outside the root-level set and, for each $N$, is bounded by a constant divided by $\mathrm{rootSizeProd}^{t}(1+\mathrm{archRootSum})^{N}$), and let $v \in S$ be a place at which every non-zero element $F$ of the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$-translates of the local factor $X.\mathrm{whittakerLoc}\,v$ has that local factor in its own such span. Then for every $W'$ in that span there exist cubic induction data $Y$ satisfying `IsCubicInductionDataOn` for the same $K$, pins, $\psi$, $\mu$ and $S$, whose local factor at $v$ is $W'$, whose local factors at all other places, archimedean Whittaker function and central character agree with those of $X$, and whose form, Whittaker and dual Whittaker functions are again continuous, with the latter two gauge-majorised.
--
--   This is the local exchange step for cubic induction data: within the cyclic module generated by the local Whittaker factor at a place of the ramification set, the factor may be replaced by any element of that module without disturbing the global automorphy, cuspidality, expansion, factorisation, growth and majorisation laws. It is used in the construction of cubic induction data with prescribed archimedean and torus behaviour at bad local packages.
